= Petit FatFs

This is a copy of Petit FatFs, a FAT file system module for systems with very
tight code space or working memory, by ChaN.
See https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/00index_p.html.

Please submit upstream bug reports to the
https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/bd/[FatFs User Forum], not to this repo.

== Releases

Each official release archive is imported in a separate commit and tagged with
its upstream version: R0.01a, R0.02, R0.02a, R0.03 and R0.03a. Commit messages
record the archive URL and SHA-256. Older `src` and `doc` directories are named
`source` and `documents`; their file contents are preserved.

This repository is Petit-only. The mixed https://github.com/pabigot/FatFs[release
mirror] was used as a provenance reference, not as the source of this history.
Some archives have been repackaged since that mirror's imports, so historical
ZIP checksums can differ; the current official archive checksum is recorded.

The repository README is added after the first upstream import and retained in
subsequent releases. XMOS build configuration and storage adapters belong in the
consuming library.

== Tags

Tags follow the same scheme as https://github.com/xmosforks/FatFs[xmosforks/FatFs]:

`R<version>`:: The pristine upstream release archive, for example `R0.03a`.
`R<version>.post<N>`:: That release with upstream's official patches 1 to N
applied, for example `R0.03a.post1`. Each patch is a separate commit titled
`R<version> patch <N>`, carrying the upstream description and the patch source.
`R<version>[.post<N>]+xmos.<M>`:: XMOS source changes on top of either of the
above. None exist at present.

The `.post<N>` and `+xmos.<M>` suffixes borrow the post-release and local
version spellings of PEP 440; the upstream version itself is not PEP 440
compliant. README-only commits are not tagged. Consuming libraries pin one of
these tags.

== Patches

The https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/pfpatches.html[known-problems page] lists one
patch for R0.03a, `pff3a_p1.diff` of May 20, 2021. It restores the missing final
row of the CP857 conversion table and removes a compiler warning when FAT32 is
disabled. It is applied to `source/pff.c` in a separate commit after the pristine
R0.03a import and tagged `R0.03a.post1`; the `R0.03a` tag remains the unpatched
archive.

The patch download on elm-chan.org returned HTTP 404 when this history was
prepared. The applied file is the Internet Archive capture of that URL,
https://web.archive.org/web/20220823043547/http://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/patch/pff3a_p1.diff
(SHA-256 `c8e8b6124fcec055d325a804624c8665f1eebeccde93abbdc7544c7b3f4d5369`).
No official checksum is published to compare it against. The patch has LF line
endings; the patched lines are stored with CRLF to match the rest of the file.

